#: ../../../index.md:1
msgid "xlwings - Make Excel Fly!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:3
msgid ""
"xlwings (Open Source) is a [BSD-licensed](http://opensource.org/licenses/"
"BSD-3-Clause) Python library that makes it easy to call Python from Excel "
"and vice versa:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:5
msgid ""
"**Scripting**: Automate/interact with Excel from Python using a syntax close "
"to VBA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:6
msgid "**Macros**: Replace VBA macros with clean and powerful Python code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:7
msgid "**UDFs**: Write User Defined Functions (UDFs) in Python (Windows only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:9
msgid ""
"**Numpy arrays** and **Pandas Series/DataFrames** are fully supported. "
"xlwings-powered workbooks are easy to distribute and work on **Windows** and "
"**Mac**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:16
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:20
msgid ""
"Start here if you are new to xlwings. Learn about the syntax, the "
"`RunPython` call, the add-in and UDFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:23
msgid "Advanced Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:27
msgid ""
"More in-depths explanations about converters, debugging or how to write your "
"own add-in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:30
msgid "xlwings Lite & xlwings Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:32
msgid "To run xlwings without having to install Python, you have two options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:34
msgid ""
"[xlwings Lite](https://lite.xlwings.org): Install the free add-in from "
"Excel's add-in store and you're done. It comes with a VS Code-like editor "
"and Wingman, a powerful AI assistant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.md:35
msgid ""
"[xlwings Server](https://server.xlwings.org): Create your own modern Excel "
"add-in with Python instead of JavaScript. Python runs on your own server and "
"comes with enterprise features such as SSO and RBAC."
msgstr ""

